{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (Task ID: 5573) to implement srd098-pinky R2.1, R2.2, and R2.3 in the go-unix-utils project. Specifically:\n   - **R2.1**: Add `-l` flag for long format output showing login name, real name (from GECOS), terminal, idle time, login time, office location, and office phone from the passwd entry.\n   - **R2.2**: Add `-f` flag to suppress the header line in short format output.\n   - **R2.3**: Add `-b` flag to suppress home directory and shell in long format, `-h` flag to suppress the project file, `-p` flag to suppress the plan file.\n   \n   The only file to modify is `cmd/pinky/main.go`. Acceptance criteria require it compiles (`go build -o bin/pinky ./cmd/pinky/`), passes `go vet`, and implements the three requirements per the SRD.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - cgo for utmpx database access and passwd lookups (`getutxent`, `getpwnam`)\n   - GECOS field parsing (comma-separated: real name, office, office phone, home phone)\n   - GNU pinky short vs long format output\n   - Differential testing against `gpinky` reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - 40-line function limit (E8), 500-line file limit (E9)\n   - Non-goal: pinky does NOT read .plan or .project files on macOS, so `-h` and `-p` flags are accepted but effectively no-ops\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd098-pinky.yaml** — The SRD defining all requirements. Key details:\n     - R2.1: `-l` long format with GECOS fields (real name, office, office phone)\n     - R2.2: `-f` suppresses header in short format\n     - R2.3: `-b` suppresses home dir/shell in long format; `-h` suppresses project file; `-p` suppresses plan file\n     - Non-goal: does not read .plan/.project files on macOS\n   \n   - **cmd/pinky/main.go** (existing, 186 lines) — Current implementation handles R1.1, R1.2, R1.3 only. Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd098-pinky R1.1, R1.2, R1.3.\n     package main\n     \n     /*\n     #include <utmpx.h>\n     #include <pwd.h>\n     #include <stdlib.h>\n     */\n     import \"C\"\n     \n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"time\"\n         \"unsafe\"\n     \n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const helpText = `Usage: pinky [OPTION]... [USER]...\n     \n       -s     do short format output, this is the default\n           --help     display this help and exit\n           --version  output version information and exit\n     \n     A lightweight 'finger' program;  print user information.\n     The utmp file will be /var/run/utmpx.\n     `\n     \n     const versionText = `pinky (go-unix-utils) dev\n     `\n     \n     type utmpEntry struct {\n         user string\n         line string\n         host string\n         time int64\n     }\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         users := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         if err := printShort(users); err != nil {\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func parseArgs(args []string) []string {\n         var users []string\n         endOfFlags := false\n         for _, arg := range args {\n             if endOfFlags {\n                 users = append(users, arg)\n                 continue\n             }\n             switch {\n             case arg == \"--help\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case arg == \"--version\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case arg == \"--\":\n                 endOfFlags = true\n             case strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\"):\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"pinky: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", arg)\n                 fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'pinky --help' for more information.\")\n                 os.Exit(1)\n             case strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") && len(arg) > 1:\n                 parseFlagBundle(arg[1:])\n             default:\n                 users = append(users, arg)\n             }\n         }\n         return users\n     }\n     \n     func parseFlagBundle(flags string) {\n         for _, ch := range flags {\n             switch ch {\n             case 's':\n                 // -s forces short format, which is the default.\n             default:\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"pinky: invalid option -- '%c'\\n\", ch)\n                 fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'pinky --help' for more information.\")\n                 os.Exit(1)\n             }\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func printShort(users []string) error {\n         entries := readEntries(users)\n         hdr := fmt.Sprintf(\"%-9s%-21s%-9s%-7s%-17s%s\",\n             \"Login\", \"Name\", \"TTY\", \"Idle\", \"When\", \"Where\")\n         if _, err := fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, hdr); err != nil {\n             return err\n         }\n         for _, e := range entries {\n             if err := printEntry(e); err != nil {\n                 return err\n             }\n         }\n         return nil\n     }\n     \n     func printEntry(e utmpEntry) error {\n         name := lookupGecos(e.user)\n         idle := idleString(e.line)\n         when := formatLoginTime(e.time)\n         var line string\n         if e.host != \"\" {\n             line = fmt.Sprintf(\"%-9s%-21s%-9s%-7s%-17s%s\",\n                 e.user, name, e.line, idle, when, e.host)\n         } else {\n             line = fmt.Sprintf(\"%-9s%-21s%-9s%-7s%s\",\n                 e.user, name, e.line, idle, when)\n         }\n         _, err := fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, line)\n         return err\n     }\n     \n     func readEntries(users []string) []utmpEntry {\n         C.setutxent()\n         defer C.endutxent()\n         filter := make(map[string]bool, len(users))\n         for _, u := range users {\n             filter[u] = true\n         }\n         var entries []utmpEntry\n         for {\n             ent := C.getutxent()\n             if ent == nil {\n                 break\n             }\n             if ent.ut_type != C.USER_PROCESS {\n                 continue\n             }\n             user := C.GoString(&ent.ut_user[0])\n             if len(filter) > 0 && !filter[user] {\n                 continue\n             }\n             entries = append(entries, utmpEntry{\n                 user: user,\n                 line: C.GoString(&ent.ut_line[0]),\n                 host: C.GoString(&ent.ut_host[0]),\n                 time: int64(ent.ut_tv.tv_sec),\n             })\n         }\n         return entries\n     }\n     \n     func idleString(ttyName string) string {\n         fi, err := sys.Stat(\"/dev/\" + ttyName)\n         if err != nil {\n             return \"?\"\n         }\n         secs := int(time.Since(fi.AccessTime).Seconds())\n         if secs < 60 {\n             return \"\"\n         }\n         if secs < 24*60*60 {\n             return fmt.Sprintf(\"%02d:%02d\", secs/3600, (secs%3600)/60)\n         }\n         return fmt.Sprintf(\"%dd\", secs/(24*60*60))\n     }\n     \n     func formatLoginTime(sec int64) string {\n         return time.Unix(sec, 0).Format(\"2006-01-02 15:04\")\n     }\n     \n     func lookupGecos(user string) string {\n         cuser := C.CString(user)\n         defer C.free(unsafe.Pointer(cuser))\n         pw := C.getpwnam(cuser)\n         if pw == nil {\n             return \"???\"\n         }\n         gecos := C.GoString(pw.pw_gecos)\n         name, _, _ := strings.Cut(gecos, \",\")\n         return name\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Err