output more carefully, the `2d1` notation indicates that line 2 from my output needs to be deleted to match gpinky's output, which means I'm printing an extra blank line that shouldn't be there. So either the trailing `putchar('\\n')` doesn't exist in the actual code, or it's only executed under certain conditions. I'm realizing the trailing empty line is only printed when the password entry exists—that's when there's additional information like Directory and Shell to display. For nonexistent users where pw is NULL, there's no trailing newline. Let me adjust the code to handle this conditional behavior.\n\nNow I need to verify what happens with the -b flag when pw exists but the Directory line gets suppressed—does gpinky still print that trailing newline?\n\nRefining the output logic... Looking at the test results, the trailing newline gets printed whenever a user exists, regardless of the `-b` flag. For nonexistent users where `pw == NULL`, there's no trailing newline at all. So I need to move that final newline print inside the `pw != nil` block so it only outputs when we actually have user data to display.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":570,"cache_read_input_tokens":69632,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":570},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"119fe2e3-5789-4d78-b7cd-29c40046ab55","uuid":"06995364-1e28-457e-a96b-3ed370b9b8bd"}
